  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a series LCR circuit, the inductance, capacitance and resistance are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> respectively. They are connected to an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AC</mi></math> source of voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and frequency of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. The approximate value of current in the circuit will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/837d7654-afbd-4673-8886-887dd9e77e78-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 145px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "22",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Angular frequency,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Here, inductive reactance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>And capacitive reactance<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Now, impedance of the series circuit is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>RMS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>RMS</mi></msub><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>220</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p>",
